cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "toolbouncer: a bouncer at the door between an agent and its tools"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - name: "Naeemeh Yadollahpour"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Naeemeh146/toolbouncer"
abstract: >-
  Call-time security enforcement for LLM agent tool use: allowlists,
  tool-description fingerprinting (rug-pull detection), least-privilege
  scopes, argument rules, and Rule-of-Two / lethal-trifecta egress
  control, with a full audit log and a bundled 20-scenario attack suite.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - mcp
  - tool-use-security
  - prompt-injection
  - guardrails
